# Testing

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`. Tests follow the same boundaries as production code.

## TypeScript

Cover: domain, application, API, repositories, integration, event processing.

Also: tool allowlist/authorization and rejection of invalid AI payloads at `AIServicePort`. Do not unit-test prompts, agents, RAG graphs, LangChain, LangGraph, or LlamaIndex in `apps/api`.

TypeScript: Vitest.

## Python

Cover: AI domain, orchestration, agents, RAG, retrieval, prompts, tool calling, guardrails, LLM adapters, AI evaluation.

Python AI (`apps/ai`): pytest. Fake `LLMPort` / `EmbeddingPort` / `VectorSearchPort`. Do not require real LLM calls in normal unit tests.

## Unit

Domain entities, value objects, domain services, use cases, business rules (TypeScript) and AI domain/orchestration (Python).

Fake ports. Do not boot Postgres, Redis, or HTTP. Do not import Prisma or LLM SDKs.

## Integration

TypeScript: repository adapters, database, queues, outbound adapters including `PythonAIServiceAdapter`. Assert mapping between Prisma records and domain entities, tenant predicates, and idempotent consumers.

Python: LLM / embedding / vector adapters with fakes or explicit provider contract tests — not TypeScript Prisma.

## E2E / API

Authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, API contracts, important workflows (create conversation, escalate, ticket resolve). Cross-runtime checks: TypeScript requests or enqueues AI work; Python returns a validated payload; TypeScript applies business state.

## Rule

A failing domain test should not require a running database. A TypeScript domain test that needs Prisma is in the wrong layer. A Python AI domain test that needs OpenAI is in the wrong layer.
